## Two parts soldered into one: programs/solder.cell run by the simulator
## -- arm A puts a DIP-8 in the vise and holds a resistor's lead to pin 3,
## arm C's iron heats the joint, arm D feeds solder, the joint freezes
## good; A lets the resistor go (it stays, soldered on), picks the DIP
## out of the vise and lifts the pair -- each command's outcome a line.
## Title: The assembly cell solders
## Page: cell/live/?program=solder watch it solder, step by step, live
## Feature: Open the cell: watch a resistor soldered to a chip a command at a time, or drive it yourself, in your browser
## Run: just demo cell solder

"ce:" u_se< "Cell"
"bl:" u_se< "Blender"

"each command: ok, its end time, what happened (the joint as it froze)"
ce:r_un bl:r_ead "programs/solder.cell"
